#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:1
#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:5
msgid "**Social Engineering Attacks**"
msgstr "Attaque par ingénierie sociale"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:7
msgid ""
"Social engineering is the manipulation of people to gain unauthorized "
"access, steal information, or trick victims into performing harmful actions. "
"Instead of exploiting technical flaws, it exploits **human weaknesses** such "
"as trust, curiosity, fear, or urgency."
msgstr ""
"L’ingénierie sociale est la manipulation des personnes pour obtenir un accès "
"non autorisé, voler des informations ou tromper les victimes afin qu’elles "
"effectuent des actions nuisibles. Au lieu d’exploiter des failles "
"techniques, elle exploite les **faiblesses humaines** telles que la "
"confiance, la curiosité, la peur ou l’urgence."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:10
msgid "**• Phishing**"
msgstr "**• Phishing**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:12
msgid ""
"Mass fraudulent emails or messages designed to trick users into clicking "
"malicious links or giving away credentials."
msgstr ""
"Emails ou messages frauduleux massifs conçus pour tromper les utilisateurs "
"afin qu’ils cliquent surlinks malveillants ou divulguent leurs identifiants."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:14
msgid "**• Spear‑Phishing**"
msgstr "**• Spear‑Phishing**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:16
msgid ""
"Highly targeted phishing aimed at specific individuals, executives, or "
"departments."
msgstr ""
"Phishing hautement ciblé visant des individus spécifiques, des cadres ou des "
"départements."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:18
msgid "**• Pretexting**"
msgstr "**• Pretexting**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:20
msgid ""
"Crafting a believable false identity or story to obtain information (e.g., "
"pretending to be an IT technician)."
msgstr ""
"Créer une fausse identité ou une histoire crédible pour obtenir des "
"informations (par ex., prétendre être un technicien informatique)."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:22
msgid "**• Baiting**"
msgstr "**• Baiting**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:24
msgid ""
"Using something tempting (free downloads, USB drives, giveaways) to lure "
"victims into a trap."
msgstr ""
"Utiliser quelque chose de tentant (téléchargements gratuits, clés USB, "
"cadeaux) pour attirer les victimes dans un piège."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:26
msgid "**• Tailgating (Piggybacking)**"
msgstr "**• Tailgating (Piggybacking)**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:28
msgid ""
"Physically following authorized personnel into restricted areas without "
"valid access."
msgstr ""
"Suivre physiquement du personnel autorisé dans des zones restreintes sans "
"accès valide."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:32
msgid "🏆 **Top 10 Biggest / Most Significant Social Engineering Incidents**"
msgstr ""
"🏆 **Top 10 des incidents d’ingénierie sociale les plus importants / "
"significatifs**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:34
msgid "High‑level, historical, and defensive-oriented."
msgstr "De haut niveau, historiques et orientés sur la défense."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:36
msgid "1. Google & Facebook Invoice Scam (~$100M, 2013–2015)"
msgstr "1. Escroquerie aux factures Google & Facebook (~100 M$, 2013–2015)"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:38
msgid ""
"Attackers impersonated a legitimate hardware supplier and tricked accounting "
"departments into sending over $100M in payments."
msgstr ""
"Les attaquants se sont fait passer pour un fournisseur de matériel légitime "
"et ont trompé les départements comptables pour envoyer plus de 100 M$ de "
"paiements."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:40
msgid "**2. RSA Security Breach (2011)**"
msgstr "**2. Violation de sécurité RSA (2011)**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:42
msgid ""
"Phishing emails with a malicious Excel file compromised RSA’s SecurID "
"system, impacting major corporations and government agencies."
msgstr ""
"Des emails de phishing contenant un fichier Excel malveillant ont compromis "
"le système SecurID de RSA, affectant de grandes entreprises et des agences "
"gouvernementales."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:44
msgid "**3. Ubiquiti Networks BEC Fraud ($40M, 2015)**"
msgstr "**3. Fraude BEC chez Ubiquiti Networks (40 M$, 2015)**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:46
msgid ""
"Attackers impersonated company executives to authorize fraudulent financial "
"transfers."
msgstr ""
"Les attaquants se sont fait passer pour des dirigeants de l’entreprise pour "
"autoriser des transferts financiers frauduleux."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:48
msgid "**4. Target Breach Entry Point (2013)**"
msgstr "**4. Point d’entrée de la violation Target (2013)**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:50
msgid ""
"Attackers stole vendor credentials through phishing, enabling access to "
"Target’s network and exposing over 40 million payment cards."
msgstr ""
"Les attaquants ont volé les identifiants des fournisseurs via phishing, "
"permettant l’accès au réseau de Target et exposant plus de 40 millions de "
"cartes de paiement."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:52
msgid "**5. 2020 Twitter Admin Panel Breach**"
msgstr "**5. Violation du panneau d’administration Twitter (2020)**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:54
msgid ""
"Teens social‑engineered Twitter employees, gaining control over internal "
"tools and major verified accounts."
msgstr ""
"Des adolescents ont utilisé l’ingénierie sociale sur des employés de "
"Twitter, prenant le contrôle des outils internes et de comptes vérifiés "
"importants."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:56
msgid "**6. Sony Pictures Hack (2014)**"
msgstr "**6. Piratage de Sony Pictures (2014)**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:58
msgid ""
"The attack began with phishing emails that led to credential theft, allowing "
"hackers to steal massive amounts of data."
msgstr ""
"L’attaque a commencé par des emails de phishing conduisant au vol "
"d’identifiants, permettant aux hackers de dérober d’énormes quantités de "
"données."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:60
msgid "**7. Snapchat Payroll Scam (2016)**"
msgstr "**7. Escroquerie sur la paie Snapchat (2016)**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:62
msgid ""
"A fake request from the CEO tricked HR into sending employee payroll "
"information."
msgstr ""
"Une fausse demande du PDG a trompé les RH pour qu’elles envoient les "
"informations sur la paie des employés."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:64
msgid "**8. FACC Aerospace CEO Fraud ($50M, 2016)**"
msgstr "**8. Fraude du PDG chez FACC Aerospace (50 M$, 2016)**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:66
msgid ""
"An email impersonating the CEO caused the company to transfer tens of "
"millions to criminals."
msgstr ""
"Un email se faisant passer pour le PDG a poussé l’entreprise à transférer "
"des dizaines de millions à des criminels."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:68
msgid "**9. Google Docs Worm (2017)**"
msgstr "**9. Ver Google Docs (2017)**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:70
msgid ""
"Millions received a fake Google Docs sharing message that attempted to gain "
"access to their contacts and spread further."
msgstr ""
"Des millions de personnes ont reçu un faux message de partage Google Docs "
"visant à accéder à leurs contacts et à se propager davantage."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:72
msgid "**10. Colonial Pipeline Initial Compromise (2021)**"
msgstr "**10. Compromission initiale de Colonial Pipeline (2021)**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:74
msgid ""
"The ransomware event stemmed from a compromised user account—believed to "
"have originated from prior phishing or password exposure."
msgstr ""
"L’événement de ransomware a découlé d’un compte utilisateur compromis, "
"probablement issu d’un phishing antérieur ou d’une exposition de mot de "
"passe."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:78
msgid "⭐ **Social Engineering “Must-Know” Techniques for Cybersecurity**"
msgstr ""
"⭐ **Techniques d’ingénierie sociale « à connaître » pour la cybersécurité**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:80
msgid "**Common Tactics**"
msgstr "**Tactiques courantes**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:82
msgid "**Urgency Pressure** (“Your account will be closed in 24 hours!”)"
msgstr "**Pression d’urgence** (« Votre compte sera fermé dans 24 heures ! »)"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:84
msgid "**Authority Impersonation** (CEO, IT support, law enforcement, vendors)"
msgstr ""
"**Imitation d’autorité** (PDG, support informatique, forces de l’ordre, "
"fournisseurs)"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:86
msgid "**Fear and Threats** (“Your tax refund is frozen unless…”)"
msgstr ""
"**Peur et menaces** (« Votre remboursement d’impôt est gelé sauf si… »)"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:88
msgid "**Curiosity Hooks** (“Look at these photos of you!”)"
msgstr "**Appâts à la curiosité** (« Regardez ces photos de vous ! »)"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:90
msgid "**Greed / Incentive Hooks** (“You’ve won a free iPhone!”)"
msgstr ""
"**Appâts à la cupidité / aux incitations** (« Vous avez gagné un iPhone "
"gratuit ! »)"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:93
msgid "**Major Social Engineering Channels**"
msgstr "**Principaux canaux d’ingénierie sociale**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:95
msgid "Email (phishing, spear‑phishing)"
msgstr "Email (phishing, spear‑phishing)"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:96
msgid "SMS (smishing)"
msgstr "SMS (smishing)"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:97
msgid "Phone calls (vishing)"
msgstr "Appels téléphoniques (vishing)"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:98
msgid "Social media impersonation"
msgstr "Usurpation sur les réseaux sociaux"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:99
msgid "USB drop attacks"
msgstr "Attaques par clé USB déposée"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:100
msgid "Physical access/social presence"
msgstr "Accès physique / présence sociale"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:102
msgid "**Organizational-Level Threats**"
msgstr "**Menaces au niveau organisationnel**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:104
msgid ""
"**Business Email Compromise (BEC)** Executive impersonation to authorize "
"fraudulent transfers."
msgstr ""
"**Compromission de messagerie d’entreprise (BEC)** Imitation de dirigeants "
"pour autoriser des transferts frauduleux."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:106
msgid ""
"**Vendor/Third-Party Compromise** Attacking suppliers to bypass stronger "
"internal defenses."
msgstr ""
"**Compromission de fournisseurs / tiers** Attaquer les fournisseurs pour "
"contourner des défenses internes plus solides."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:108
msgid ""
"**Insider Manipulation** Convincing employees to share credentials or system "
"access."
msgstr ""
"**Manipulation interne** Convaincre les employés de partager des "
"identifiants ou l’accès au système."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:113
msgid "**Phishing – Focuses & Variants**"
msgstr "**Phishing – Axes et variantes**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:115
msgid "**Major Phishing Types**"
msgstr "**Principaux types de phishing**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:117
msgid "**Standard Phishing** – Mass emails."
msgstr "**Phishing standard** – Emails massifs."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:118
msgid "**Spear‑Phishing** – Targeted individuals."
msgstr "**Spear‑Phishing** – Individus ciblés."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:119
msgid "**Whaling** – Targeting high-value executives."
msgstr "**Whaling** – Cibler des cadres de haute valeur."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:120
msgid "**Smishing** – Fraudulent SMS messages."
msgstr "**Smishing** – Messages SMS frauduleux."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:121
msgid "**Vishing** – Phone call–based social engineering."
msgstr "**Vishing** – Ingénierie sociale par appels téléphoniques."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:122
msgid ""
"**Clone Phishing** – Re-sending legitimate emails with malicious payloads."
msgstr ""
"**Clone Phishing** – Renvoi d’emails légitimes avec charges malveillantes."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:124
msgid "**Well-Known Phishing Examples**"
msgstr "**Exemples célèbres de phishing**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:126
msgid "Google & Facebook scam"
msgstr "Escroquerie Google & Facebook"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:127
msgid "RSA breach"
msgstr "Violation RSA"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:128
msgid "Ubiquiti BEC"
msgstr "BEC chez Ubiquiti"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:129
msgid "Google Docs worm"
msgstr "Ver Google Docs"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/social_engineering.md:130
msgid "PayPal/banking phishing kits (ongoing)"
msgstr "Kits de phishing PayPal / bancaire (en cours)"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:1
msgid "**Malware‑Based Attacks**"
msgstr "**Attaques basées sur les malwares**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:3
msgid ""
"Malware (**malicious software**) refers to any software intentionally "
"created to damage systems, disrupt operations, steal data, or gain "
"unauthorized access. Malware attacks remain one of the most common and "
"destructive cybersecurity threats."
msgstr ""
"Les malwares (**logiciels malveillants**) désignent tout logiciel créé "
"intentionnellement pour endommager les systèmes, perturber les opérations, "
"voler des données ou obtenir un accès non autorisé. Les attaques par malware "
"restent l’une des menaces de cybersécurité les plus courantes et "
"destructrices."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:7
msgid "**Types of Malware**"
msgstr "**Types de malwares**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:9
msgid "**• Viruses**"
msgstr "**• Virus**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:11
msgid ""
"Malicious code that attaches to legitimate files and spreads when they are "
"executed."
msgstr ""
"Code malveillant qui s’attache à des fichiers légitimes et se propage "
"lorsqu’ils sont exécutés."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:13
msgid "**• Worms**"
msgstr "**• Vers**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:15
msgid ""
"Self‑replicating malware that spreads automatically across networks without "
"user action."
msgstr ""
"Malware auto-réplicatif qui se propage automatiquement à travers les réseaux "
"sans action de l’utilisateur."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:17
msgid "**• Trojans**"
msgstr "**• Troyens**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:19
msgid ""
"Malware disguised as a legitimate file or application to trick users into "
"installing it."
msgstr ""
"Malware déguisé en fichier ou application légitime pour tromper les "
"utilisateurs et les inciter à l’installer."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:21
msgid "**• Ransomware**"
msgstr "**• Ransomware**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:23
msgid ""
"Malware that encrypts files or systems and demands payment for decryption."
msgstr ""
"Malware qui chiffre des fichiers ou des systèmes et exige un paiement pour "
"les déchiffrer."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:25
msgid "**• Spyware / Keyloggers**"
msgstr "**• Spyware / Keyloggers**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:27
msgid ""
"Software that covertly monitors user activity, capturing keystrokes or "
"sensitive data."
msgstr ""
"Logiciel qui surveille discrètement l’activité des utilisateurs, capturant "
"les frappes au clavier ou des données sensibles."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:29
msgid "**• Adware**"
msgstr "**• Adware**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:31
msgid ""
"Software that displays unwanted ads or redirects users; sometimes used to "
"track users or degrade system performance."
msgstr ""
"Logiciel affichant des publicités indésirables ou redirigeant les "
"utilisateurs ; parfois utilisé pour suivre les utilisateurs ou dégrader les "
"performances du système."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:35
msgid "🏆 **Top 10 Most Significant Malware Attacks (All‑Time)**"
msgstr ""
"🏆 **Top 10 des attaques par malware les plus significatives (tous temps)**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:37
msgid "**1. WannaCry (2017)**"
msgstr "**1. WannaCry (2017)**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:39
msgid ""
"A global ransomware worm that infected 200,000+ systems in 150 countries, "
"crippling hospitals, telecoms, and manufacturing."
msgstr ""
"Un ver ransomware mondial qui a infecté plus de 200 000 systèmes dans 150 "
"pays, paralysant hôpitaux, télécoms et industries."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:41
msgid "**2. NotPetya (2017)**"
msgstr "**2. NotPetya (2017)**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:43
msgid ""
"A destructive wiper disguised as ransomware, causing over **$10 billion** in "
"damages worldwide. Spread through poisoned software updates."
msgstr ""
"Un wiper destructeur déguisé en ransomware, causant plus de **10 milliards "
"de $** de dommages dans le monde. Propagé via des mises à jour logicielles "
"compromises."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:45
msgid "**3. Stuxnet (2010)**"
msgstr "**3. Stuxnet (2010)**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:47
msgid ""
"A sophisticated worm targeting industrial systems (ICS/SCADA). It physically "
"damaged Iran’s nuclear centrifuges—considered a landmark cyber‑physical "
"attack."
msgstr ""
"Un ver sophistiqué ciblant les systèmes industriels (ICS/SCADA). Il a "
"endommagé physiquement les centrifugeuses nucléaires iraniennes — considéré "
"comme une attaque cyber‑physique majeure."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:49
msgid "**4. ILoveYou Virus (2000)**"
msgstr "**4. Virus ILoveYou (2000)**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:51
msgid ""
"One of the fastest‑spreading viruses ever, spreading via email and causing "
"billions in losses."
msgstr ""
"Un des virus les plus rapides à se propager, se diffusant par email et "
"causant des milliards de pertes."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:53
msgid "**5. SQL Slammer Worm (2003)**"
msgstr "**5. Ver SQL Slammer (2003)**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:55
msgid ""
"A tiny worm (376 bytes!) that spread across the internet in minutes, "
"knocking out ATMs, airlines, and emergency services."
msgstr ""
"Un petit ver (376 octets !) qui s’est propagé sur Internet en quelques "
"minutes, paralysant distributeurs automatiques, compagnies aériennes et "
"services d’urgence."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:57
msgid "**6. Code Red (2001)**"
msgstr "**6. Code Red (2001)**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:59
msgid ""
"A worm targeting Windows servers, defacing websites and launching major DDoS "
"attacks."
msgstr ""
"Un ver ciblant les serveurs Windows, défigurant des sites web et lançant "
"d’importantes attaques DDoS."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:61
msgid "**7. Zeus Trojan (2007–present)**"
msgstr "**7. Troyen Zeus (2007–présent)**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:63
msgid ""
"A banking trojan used for massive credential theft and online fraud. Spawned "
"numerous variants."
msgstr ""
"Un troyen bancaire utilisé pour le vol massif d’identifiants et la fraude en "
"ligne. A donné naissance à de nombreuses variantes."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:65
msgid "**8. Conficker (2008)**"
msgstr "**8. Conficker (2008)**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:67
msgid ""
"Infected millions of systems through Windows vulnerabilities and weak "
"passwords. A major wake‑up call for patching."
msgstr ""
"A infecté des millions de systèmes via des vulnérabilités Windows et des "
"mots de passe faibles. Un signal fort pour l’importance des correctifs."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:69
msgid "**9. CryptoLocker (2013)**"
msgstr "**9. CryptoLocker (2013)**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:71
msgid ""
"One of the first successful modern ransomware campaigns—popularized the “pay "
"to decrypt” model still common today."
msgstr ""
"Une des premières campagnes de ransomware modernes réussies — popularisant "
"le modèle « payer pour déchiffrer » encore courant aujourd’hui."

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:73
msgid "**10. Emotet (2014–2021, revived 2021)**"
msgstr "**10. Emotet (2014–2021, relancé 2021)**"

#: src/cybersecurity/attacks/malware.md:75
